# Michelle, intro (figure 82.1)
# A held C on top over a chromatic inner line F E Eb D Db C, all on an f-minor "envelope" until
# the V (a bare open fifth on C) in bar 4. Timing in bars 1-3 follows the column positions of the
# typed chart (E on beat 4 of bar 1; D on beat 3 of bar 2; in bar 3, C on beat 2, Bb on its "and",
# Ab from the "and" of beat 3).
# Pollack's footnote: iv 6/5 here can alternately be parsed as vi 4/3 (D-flat) by virtue of the F
# in the bass (the low F he says enters at the start of bar 3; he doesn't type it in the chart).
#? Bar 3 melody rhythm (C beat 2, Bb on the "and" of 2, Ab on the "and" of 3) is read from spacing only.
meter 4/4
key f

system
voice "Melody"       | C5 | - |
voice "Inner line"   | F4*3 E4 | Eb4*2 D4*2 |
chords "Chords"      | f{i} | - |

system
